{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_5ba1019b4335445e856895fc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the controller's test style. The tests use `Expect` inside httptest handlers (this works because the request is handled synchronously during the client's Do call in the same goroutine — actually httptest handlers run in a separate goroutine, but Ginkgo supports assertions from goroutines via its registered `Fail` — the failure gets propagated via `gomega`'s `Gomega` object which captures failures and reports them; in Ginkgo v2 it can be flaky but this is the established pattern in the controller repo, and it's what the prompt asks to mirror).\n\nActually, let me be careful. The controller tests use `Expect` inside the handler, and those pass. Ginkgo v2's Gomega with the default global `Expect` works in goroutines — failures will call `Fail`, which in Ginkgo v2 is safe to call from goroutines (it records the failure). So I'll mirror the style but I'll use captured variables where the requirement wants assertions on headers, following the controller's approach of capturing into variables and asserting after the call (safer).\n\nLet me design the test file for our port:\n\n```go\npackage gitrestclient_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"net/http/httptest\"\n\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n\n\t\"github.com/bborbe/agent-task-executor/pkg/gitrestclient\"\n)\n\nvar _ = Describe(\"GitRestClient\", func() {\n\tvar (\n\t\tctx    context.Context\n\t\tserver *httptest.Server\n\t\tclient gitrestclient.GitRestClient\n\t)\n\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tctx = context.Background()\n\t\tserver = nil\n\t})\n\n\tAfterEach(func() {\n\t\tif server != nil {\n\t\t\tserver.Close()\n\t\t}\n\t})\n\n\tDescribe(\"Get\", func() {\n\t\tContext(\"200 response\", func() {\n\t\t\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\t\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(r.Method).To(Equal(http.MethodGet))\n\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(r.URL.Path).To(Equal(\"/api/v1/files/tasks/foo.md\"))\n\t\t\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"---\\nfoo: bar\\n---\\nbody\"))\n\t\t\t\t\t}),\n\t\t\t\t)\n\t\t\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t\t\t})\n\n\t\t\tIt(\"returns the file bytes and nil error\", func() {\n\t\t\t\tcontent, err := client.Get(ctx, \"tasks/foo.md\")\n\t\t\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\t\t\tExpect(content).To(Equal([]byte(\"---\\nfoo: bar\\n---\\nbody\")))\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t})\n\t\t...\n\t})\n})\n```\n\nNow, requirement (b): \"Get non-200 (404): returns an error whose message contains the status code.\" So:\n```go\nContext(\"404 response\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusNotFound)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"not found\"))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns an error containing the status code\", func() {\n\t\tcontent, err := client.Get(ctx, \"tasks/missing.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).To(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(err.Error()).To(ContainSubstring(\"404\"))\n\t\tExpect(content).To(BeNil())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(c) Get with gateway secret:\n```go\nContext(\"gateway secret configured sends auth headers\", func() {\n\tvar capturedSecret, capturedInitiator string\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tcapturedSecret = r.Header.Get(\"X-Gateway-Secret\")\n\t\t\t\tcapturedInitiator = r.Header.Get(\"X-Gateway-Initator\")\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"body\"))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"s3cret\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"sends both auth headers\", func() {\n\t\t_, err := client.Get(ctx, \"tasks/foo.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(capturedSecret).To(Equal(\"s3cret\"))\n\t\tExpect(capturedInitiator).To(Equal(\"agent-task-executor\"))\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(d) Get with empty gateway secret:\n```go\nContext(\"empty gateway secret sends no auth headers\", func() {\n\tvar capturedSecret, capturedInitiator string\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tcapturedSecret = r.Header.Get(\"X-Gateway-Secret\")\n\t\t\t\tcapturedInitiator = r.Header.Get(\"X-Gateway-Initator\")\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"body\"))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"sends neither auth header\", func() {\n\t\t_, err := client.Get(ctx, \"tasks/foo.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(capturedSecret).To(BeEmpty())\n\t\tExpect(capturedInitiator).To(BeEmpty())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(e) Get path escaping: relPath `\"24 Tasks/a b.md\"`:\n```go\nContext(\"relPath with spaces is percent-escaped\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\t// r.URL.Path is the decoded path — the space and the segment\n\t\t\t\t// separators survive as separate path elements.\n\t\t\t\tExpect(r.URL.Path).To(Equal(\"/api/v1/files/24 Tasks/a b.md\"))\n\t\t\t\t// url.PathEscape escapes the space in the URL, so the escaped\n\t\t\t\t// form carries %20.\n\t\t\t\tExpect(r.URL.EscapedPath()).To(ContainSubstring(\"%20\"))\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"ok\"))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"escapes the path and succeeds\", func() {\n\t\tcontent, err := client.Get(ctx, \"24 Tasks/a b.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(content).To(Equal([]byte(\"ok\")))\n\t})\n})\n```\n\nWait — will `r.URL.Path` be the decoded `/api/v1/files/24 Tasks/a b.md`? When the HTTP server receives the request line `GET /api/v1/files/24%20Tasks/a%20b.md HTTP/1.1`, Go's `http.ReadRequest` parses `r.URL.Path` as the decoded path. Yes — `URL.Path` is decoded, `RawPath`/`EscapedPath()` holds the escaped version. So `r.URL.Path == \"/api/v1/files/24 Tasks/a b.md\"` and `r.URL.EscapedPath() == \"/api/v1/files/24%20Tasks/a%20b.md\"`. Good.\n\n(f) List 200:\n```go\nContext(\"2 paths returned\", func() {\n\tvar receivedGlob string\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tExpect(r.Method).To(Equal(http.MethodGet))\n\t\t\t\treceivedGlob = r.URL.Query().Get(\"glob\")\n\t\t\t\tw.Header().Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(`[\"24 Tasks/a.md\",\"24 Tasks/b.md\"]`))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns the paths and propagates the glob query param\", func() {\n\t\tpaths, err := client.List(ctx, \"24 Tasks/*.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(paths).To(Equal([]string{\"24 Tasks/a.md\", \"24 Tasks/b.md\"}))\n\t\tExpect(receivedGlob).To(Equal(\"24 Tasks/*.md\"))\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(g) List non-200:\n```go\nContext(\"non-200 response\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusInternalServerError)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"internal error\"))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns an error containing the status code\", func() {\n\t\tpaths, err := client.List(ctx, \"24 Tasks/*.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).To(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(err.Error()).To(ContainSubstring(\"500\"))\n\t\tExpect(paths).To(BeNil())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(h) List unparseable body:\n```go\nContext(\"malformed JSON body\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(\"not json\"))\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns nil and a non-nil error (no panic)\", func() {\n\t\tpaths, err := client.List(ctx, \"24 Tasks/*.md\")\n\t\tExpect(err).To(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(paths).To(BeNil())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(i) IsReady 200:\n```go\nContext(\"200 response\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tExpect(r.URL.Path).To(Equal(\"/readiness\"))\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns true, nil\", func() {\n\t\tready, err := client.IsReady(ctx)\n\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(ready).To(BeTrue())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(j) IsReady 503:\n```go\nContext(\"503 response\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusServiceUnavailable)\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns false, nil — a valid not-ready state, not an error\", func() {\n\t\tready, err := client.IsReady(ctx)\n\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(ready).To(BeFalse())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(k) IsReady 500:\n```go\nContext(\"500 response\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n\t\t\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusInternalServerError)\n\t\t\t}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns false, error\", func() {\n\t\tready, err := client.IsReady(ctx)\n\t\tExpect(err).To(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(ready).To(BeFalse())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\n(l) IsReady closed server:\n```go\nContext(\"network error (stopped server)\", func() {\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tserver = httptest.NewServer(\n\t\t\thttp.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {}),\n\t\t)\n\t\tclient = gitrestclient.NewGitRestClient(server.URL, \"\", \"agent-task-executor\")\n\t\tserver.Close()\n\t\tserver = nil\n\t})\n\tIt(\"returns false, error\", func() {\n\t\tready, err := client.IsReady(ctx)\n\t\tExpect(err).To(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tExpect(ready).To(BeFalse())\n\t})\n})\n```\n\nNow, an important consideration: the `AfterEach` closes the server; in (l) we set `server = nil` after closing so AfterEach doesn't double-close (double-close is harmless anyway, but the controller pattern sets nil).\n\nOne concern: `Expect` inside the httptest handler goroutine. In Ginkgo v2, Gomega assertions from a goroutine other than the running spec goroutine: the global `Expect` registers with the global Gomega, and if it fails it calls `gomega.AddNonSuccessfulReturnedArgs`... Actually in Ginkgo v2, `Fail` can be called from any goroutine — it records the failure and aborts the spec once it returns. This is supported. The controller's tests do this and pass. Fine.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtle issue with `Expect(r.Method).To(Equal(http.MethodGet))` inside the handler: if it fails, the handler panics? Actually no — Gomega's `Expect` calls the registered failure handler which for Ginkgo is `Fail`. In Ginkgo v2, `Fail` from a non-spec goroutine is handled: it marks the spec failed. This is fine.\n\nNow let me write the test file.\n\nAlso note the requirement for `package gitrestclient_test` and the import of the gitrestclient package: `github.com/bborbe/agent-task-executor/pkg/gitrestclient`.\n\nLet me now write git_rest_client_test.go.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab2e800e-9400-4e49-90cb-78b86646bc3f","uuid":"afa3c087-6342-4b1e-a454-d1c1c35cc719","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:21:11.362Z"}
